0,Tagalaka language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tagalaka_language,"January 1, 2026 - Takalak (Tagalaka, Dagalag) is a poorly attested, extinct Australian Aboriginal language of Queensland.",Tagalaka,Australian
1,Australian Dance Theatre - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Dance_Theatre,"October 13, 2025 - It is co-created by Riley, theatre-maker S. Shakthidharan (Counting and Cracking) and Tagalaka dancer and choreographer Jasmin Sheppard. Music is by Singapore-based group SAtheCollective and Jaadwa composer James Howard, and the work includes video and text as well as dance.",Tagalaka,Australian
2,Indigenous music of Australia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigenous_music_of_Australia,"1 week ago - The traditional forms include many aspects of performance and musical instrumentation that are unique to particular regions or Aboriginal Australian groups; and some elements of musical tradition are common or widespread through much of the Australian continent, and even beyond.",Tagalaka,Australian
3,Australian folk music - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_folk_music,"July 18, 2025 - Celtic, English, German and Scandinavian folk traditions predominated in the first wave of European immigrant music. The Australian tradition is, in this sense, related to the traditions of other countries with similar ethnic, historical and political origins, such as New Zealand, Canada and ...",Tagalaka,Australian
4,Tagalag people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tagalag_people,"April 28, 2025 - The Tagalag are an Indigenous Australian tribe of Northern Queensland. The Tagalag tribal lands covered roughly 3,900 square miles (10,000 km2) around the Middle Gilbert River. Tagalaka Country covers various lands in the Gulf Savannah region around the townships of Croydon, Normanton and East ...",Tagalaka,Australian
5,The Sound of Australian Indigenous Music - playlist by The Sounds of Spotify | Spotify,https://open.spotify.com/playlist/6B9CpGm9IBQJzncRCPw0dG,Playlist · The Sound of Australian Indigenous Music · 343 items · 667 saves,Tagalaka,Australian
6,Australian Folksongs and Ballads | Smithsonian Folkways Recordings,https://folkways.si.edu/john-greenway/australian-folksongs-and-ballads/world/music/album/smithsonian,"This album gathers a variety of folksongs that tell of Australian History and folklore. Liner notes include detailed information on each song, with an introduction on Australia’s relationship to folk music.",Tagalaka,Australian
7,Australia: Aboriginal Music | Smithsonian Folkways Recordings,https://folkways.si.edu/australia-aboriginal-music/world/music/album/smithsonian,"The album includes ten songs — Rain Dreaming songs, clan songs, dance songs, and women's songs — in nine languages. The liner notes present detailed information about regional variations in the music and about each selection.",Tagalaka,Australian
8,Traditional Australian Aboriginal Music,https://www.aboriginalart.com.au/didgeridoo/,"We are a Southern Arrernte Aboriginal Tribal group whose homelands are situated 100 kms south of Alice Springs in Central Australia. Since 1995 we have owned and operated the Aboriginal Art and Culture Centre in Alice Springs · Our community has been involved in Aboriginal Music for 40,000 ...",Tagalaka,Australian
9,Australian Folk Music,https://www.wfmt.info/post/australian-folk-music,"Many of these surviving songs describe the animist belief systems (widely known as the ‘Dreamtime’ or ‘Dreaming’) that indigenous Australians follow, in which spirituality is closely related to the landscape, flora and fauna of Australia (Magowan, 2007). Two types of Ngarla songs have survived - jarlurra are corroboree songs (corroborees are Aboriginal ceremonies) and yirarru are story songs (Brown & Geytenbeek, 2003). The Yolngu are an Aboriginal tribe that inhabit north-east Arnhem Land in Australia’s Northern Territory. Music remains a strong part of Yolngu culture and they continue to pass down their traditions of music and dance orally.",Tagalaka,Australian
